From 0f5001068d2bf61e7bd554ebf69bb313aea5566c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:36:13 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 250/341] Unified: one window without modes instead of
 FreeCAD's menus and toolbars
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The menu bar is one menu, "☰": new part / assembly / drawing, files,
import and export, the tool search, other tools, and FreeCAD's Edit, View,
Tools, Macro, Window and Help menus as submenus (their shortcuts keep
working). At its right: undo, redo, the search, the AI and the preferences.
One tool strip with names under the icons stays the same whatever is
picked or open (a sketch, a drawing page, an assembly); FreeCAD's toolbars
are gone. One-key shortcuts for the strip (S sketch, E extrude, C cut out,
H hole, F fillet, M move, D measure) never fire while text is typed (a
text field has the focus or the input method composes) or while a sketch
is edited (its own keys then); other commands lose these keys.

"Other tools" lists every tool of every module by kind, as their modules
put them in menus, the specialist toolboxes (BIM, CAM, FEM, robot, ...)
last; a module is loaded when one of its tools is first used. New commands:
new part, new assembly, make drawing (the three views of the picked part
on a new sheet), put part (into the file's assembly, made if needed), and
in the right-click menu of a step: edit its sketch, insert after it (set
tip), move it. Preferences › General › Screen brings FreeCAD's menus and
toolbars back.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
